<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Systema Naturae</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1735</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Systema Naturae is the work in which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carl-linnaeus">Carl Linnaeus</a> set out his classification of nature into the three kingdoms of animals, plants and minerals, divided into classes, orders, genera and species. First published at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leiden">Leiden</a> in 1735 as a short folio, it grew through many editions, and its tenth edition of 1758 is the formal starting point of zoological nomenclature.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/systema-naturae.jpg" alt="Systema Naturae" width="320" height="517" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Carl Linnaeus · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Linnaeus1758-title-page.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
